📌 PART 1: Boot Process (1-20)
Q1. What is the first software executed after powering on a computer?

A) OS Kernel
B) BIOS/UEFI ✅
C) Bootloader
D) Shell

Why?

When power is supplied, firmware starts first.

Boot sequence:

Power On
↓
BIOS/UEFI
↓
Bootloader
↓
Kernel
↓
OS
Q2. BIOS stands for?

A) Basic Input Output System ✅
B) Binary Input Output System
C) Boot Integrated OS System
D) Basic Internal Operating Software

Why?

BIOS is firmware stored on motherboard.

Q3. Modern systems mostly use?

A) DOS
B) BIOS
C) UEFI ✅
D) FAT

Why?

UEFI is faster, secure, and supports large disks.

Q4. Which component loads the OS kernel?

A) CPU
B) Bootloader ✅
C) RAM
D) Shell

Why?

Bootloader's job is:

Find Kernel
Load Kernel
Transfer Control
Q5. Which bootloader is common in Linux?

A) NTLDR
B) GRUB ✅
C) CMD
D) Bash

Why?

GRUB = Grand Unified Bootloader.

Q6. Secure Boot prevents?

A) Virus in RAM
B) Unauthorized boot code ✅
C) Disk Fragmentation
D) Scheduling

Why?

Secure Boot verifies boot components.

Q7. UEFI replaces?

A) Kernel
B) BIOS ✅
C) Shell
D) Scheduler

Why?

UEFI is modern firmware architecture.

Q8. POST stands for?

A) Power-On Self Test ✅
B) Process Operating System Test
C) Power OS Transfer
D) Program Output State Test

Why?

Checks RAM, keyboard, CPU etc.

Q9. If POST fails, system may?

A) Boot normally
B) Shut down or beep error ✅
C) Open shell
D) Start kernel

Why?

Hardware problems detected before OS starts.

Q10. Kernel is loaded into?

A) SSD
B) Cache
C) RAM ✅
D) Register

Why?

CPU executes instructions from memory.

Q11. Which partition type is preferred by UEFI?

A) FAT16
B) MBR
C) GPT ✅
D) EXT2

Why?

GPT supports large disks and more partitions.

Q12. MBR full form?

A) Main Boot Register
B) Master Boot Record ✅
C) Memory Boot Region
D) Machine Boot Record

Why?

Stores boot information.

Q13. Kernel initialization happens after?

A) Shell
B) Scheduler
C) Bootloader ✅
D) Login

Why?

Bootloader loads kernel first.

Q14. Which firmware supports graphical interface?

A) UEFI ✅
B) BIOS
C) DOS
D) FAT

Why?

UEFI offers GUI and mouse support.

Q15. What happens before kernel starts?

A) Login
B) BIOS/UEFI and Bootloader ✅
C) Shell
D) Process Creation

Why?

Kernel cannot start itself.

Q16. Firmware is stored in?

A) RAM
B) SSD
C) ROM/Flash Memory ✅
D) Cache

Why?

Firmware must persist after shutdown.

Q17. Booting means?

A) Installing OS
B) Starting Computer and Loading OS ✅
C) Formatting Disk
D) Compiling Program

Why?

Booting loads operating system into memory.

Q18. Warm Boot means?

A) Restarting system ✅
B) First startup
C) Kernel panic
D) Shutdown

Why?

Warm boot = reboot.

Q19. Cold Boot means?

A) Restart
B) Fresh Power-On Start ✅
C) Sleep
D) Hibernate

Why?

System starts from powered-off state.

Q20. Which component transfers control to kernel?

A) Scheduler
B) Shell
C) Bootloader ✅
D) Driver

Why?

Bootloader hands execution to kernel.

